From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dinesh Choudhary <idinesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:26:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] feat(qti): enable PSCI SYSTEM_RESET2 support for nord

Nord reuses the common plat/qti/common/src/qti_pm.c and
pm_ps_hold.c PM backend (unlike hamoa, which has its own
wildcat_bl31qtilib_pm.c), so the vendor SYSTEM_RESET2 handling
already added there for hoya/bruin platforms is already reachable
for nord. Two pieces specific to nord are still missing.

Define PON_SOFT_RB_SPARE and TCSR_BOOT_MISC_DETECT for nord so the
reboot-reason cookie stash in qti_pmic_prepare_reset2() is enabled
for it, matching downstream TZ's nord ASIC reset_info_config
(0x7148) and HWIO_TCSR_BOOT_MISC_DETECT address
(TCSR_TCSR_REGS_REG_BASE + 0x99000).

Nord also has a companion SAIL die that must be given a heads-up
before a hard reset tears down PS_HOLD. A vendor hard reset via
SYSTEM_RESET2 is the same SoC-level event as the architectural
SYSTEM_RESET, so route it through the qti_sail_comm_system_reset()
call already used by qti_system_reset(), matching downstream TZ's
psci_target_system_reset2() ASIC hook, which notifies the SAIL/modem
subsystem the same way for both reset paths. Warm reset has no
downstream SAIL notification, so it is left alone.

Move the vendor sub-type mask/values from pm_ps_hold.c to qti_plat.h
so qti_pm.c can check the resolved sub-type without duplicating them.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-5
Signed-off-by: Dinesh Choudhary <idinesh@qti.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/trusted-firmware-a/pull/135]
Signed-off-by: Roshan Sivakumar <roshs@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 plat/qti/common/inc/qti_plat.h           | 10 ++++++++++
 plat/qti/common/src/pm_ps_hold.c         | 11 -----------
 plat/qti/common/src/qti_pm.c             | 10 ++++++++++
 plat/qti/wildcat/nord/inc/platform_def.h |  8 ++++++++
 4 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/qti/common/inc/qti_plat.h b/plat/qti/common/inc/qti_plat.h
index c74f73909..dd493d5d2 100644
--- a/plat/qti/common/inc/qti_plat.h
+++ b/plat/qti/common/inc/qti_plat.h
@@ -51,6 +51,16 @@ void qti_pmic_prepare_reset(void);
 void qti_pmic_prepare_shutdown(void);
 int qti_pmic_prepare_reset2(uint32_t reset_type, uint64_t cookie);
 
+/*
+ * Vendor SYSTEM_RESET2 sub-types, selected by the low bits of the PSCI
+ * reset_type argument. Mirrors the sub-types of downstream TZ's
+ * pm_app_pon_reset_cfg_type enum that the PMIC PON config actually
+ * distinguishes; any other value is rejected as unsupported.
+ */
+#define QTI_RESET2_TYPE_MASK		0x7fU
+#define QTI_PON_CFG_WARM_RESET		0
+#define QTI_PON_CFG_HARD_RESET		1
+
 int plat_qti_pwr_domain_on(u_register_t mpidr, int core_pos);
 void plat_qti_pwr_domain_on_finish(int core_pos, const uint8_t *states);
 void plat_qti_pwr_domain_off(const uint8_t *states);
diff --git a/plat/qti/common/src/pm_ps_hold.c b/plat/qti/common/src/pm_ps_hold.c
index c162da6f4..ffb58712f 100644
--- a/plat/qti/common/src/pm_ps_hold.c
+++ b/plat/qti/common/src/pm_ps_hold.c
@@ -23,17 +23,6 @@
 
 #define S2_RESET_EN			BIT(7)
 
-/*
- * Vendor SYSTEM_RESET2 sub-types, selected by the low bits of the PSCI
- * reset_type argument. Mirrors the sub-types of downstream TZ's
- * pm_app_pon_reset_cfg_type enum that shikra's PMIC PON config actually
- * distinguishes; any other value is rejected as unsupported.
- */
-#define QTI_PON_CFG_WARM_RESET		0
-#define QTI_PON_CFG_HARD_RESET		1
-
-#define QTI_RESET2_TYPE_MASK		0x7fU
-
 /* Set when the vendor payload carries a reboot-reason cookie update. */
 #define QTI_RESET2_COOKIE		BIT(16)
 
diff --git a/plat/qti/common/src/qti_pm.c b/plat/qti/common/src/qti_pm.c
index c6dd93945..1bec50ebc 100644
--- a/plat/qti/common/src/qti_pm.c
+++ b/plat/qti/common/src/qti_pm.c
@@ -230,6 +230,16 @@ static int qti_system_reset2(int is_vendor, int reset_type, u_register_t cookie)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A vendor hard reset is the same SoC-level reset as the
+	 * architectural SYSTEM_RESET, so it needs the same companion SAIL
+	 * die heads-up before PS_HOLD is deasserted. Warm reset has no
+	 * equivalent downstream SAIL notification, so it is left alone.
+	 */
+	if (((uint32_t)reset_type & QTI_RESET2_TYPE_MASK) == QTI_PON_CFG_HARD_RESET) {
+		qti_sail_comm_system_reset();
+	}
+
 	assert_ps_hold();
 }
 
diff --git a/plat/qti/wildcat/nord/inc/platform_def.h b/plat/qti/wildcat/nord/inc/platform_def.h
index ad4f67851..414f3586d 100644
--- a/plat/qti/wildcat/nord/inc/platform_def.h
+++ b/plat/qti/wildcat/nord/inc/platform_def.h
@@ -169,6 +169,14 @@
 #define QTI_PS_HOLD_REG 0xC264000
 #define PON_PS_HOLD_RESET_CTL 0x852
 #define PON_PS_HOLD_RESET_CTL2 0x853
+#define PON_SOFT_RB_SPARE 0x7148
+
+/*
+ * TCSR reboot-reason scratch register (TCSR_TCSR_REGS_REG_BASE + 0x99000,
+ * where TCSR_TCSR_REGS_REG_BASE is CORE_TOP_CSR_BASE-family but at its own
+ * offset on Nord).
+ */
+#define TCSR_BOOT_MISC_DETECT 0x01FD9000
 
 #define SPMI_ARB_APID_MAP_BASE	0x0C402000U
 #define SPMI_ARB_CHNL_BASE	0x0C500000U
